  "title": "Confusing wording in the window directing to login",
  "content": "<p>When attempting to reply or thumb-up while not logged in, a popup window appears which directs me to log in. However, the wording there is confusing to users:</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/a716046d-5ef8-47fd-8456-5e1fe776290b.png\" /></figure><p>Why would I as user be concerned with “SSO” and “Saml2?”</p><p>I recommend to remove “Login with SSO” and rename “Login with Saml2” in the button to mere “Login” or “Click here to log in”.</p><p>JW</p>",
